<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swiss peasant war of 1653</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1653">1653</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swiss peasant war of 1653 was a revolt of the rural subjects of Lucerne, Bern, Solothurn and Basel against their patrician city governments, set off by a devaluation of the currency and falling prices after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. Led by Niklaus Leuenberger, the peasants formed the League of Huttwil, but the forces of the cities defeated them at Wohlenschwil and Herzogenbuchsee, and Leuenberger and other leaders were executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swiss-peasant-war-of-1653.jpg" alt="Swiss peasant war of 1653" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lupo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Swiss_Peasant_War_of_1653.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
